WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:05.310
- Hello, welcome to Ed
Talks with Khan Academy,

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:09.380
where we talk to experts
in the field of education.

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:12.500
Today we have with us Sophie Bosmeny,

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:16.050
who is with Khan Kids
and she's gonna update us

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:18.940
on what's going on with Khan Kids

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:21.630
or up to eight year olds,

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:25.110
so we are looking forward to
hearing what she has to say.

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:27.850
Before we get started a
reminder that Khan Academy

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:31.120
is a non-profit and we rely on donations

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.510
to keep up the work that we are doing.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:38.310
So you will find at KhanAcademy.org/donate

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:41.770
the place where you can make a donation,

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:43.660
whatever you can give is appreciated

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:47.200
and thank you for helping us
to continue to do this work.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:51.120
We also wanna recognize a few companies

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:55.020
that really in the time
of COVID-19 stepped up

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:56.910
to help us make sure we could meet

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:59.860
the increasing demand for what we do.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:04.210
That includes Bank of
America, AT&amp;T, Google.org,

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:07.573
Novartis, Fastly and
General Motors, thank you.

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:13.670
And finally, if you have
missed some of these Ed Talks

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:17.750
or Homerooms you can find
us in your podcast app

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:21.170
at Homeroom with Sal and
replay the audio versions

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:23.020
of these discussions.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:26.070
So we look forward to
seeing you there as well.

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:29.510
And with that, I will welcome Sophie.

00:01:29.510 --> 00:01:32.080
Thank you for joining us today.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:34.020
- Thank you for having me, Kristen.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.690
It's great to see you
and I'm really excited

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:39.063
to be talking about Khan Academy Kids.

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:40.960
- Excellent.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:42.840
So let's start off.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:44.560
Tell us a little bit about yourself.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:46.893
What's your role at Khan Academy Kids?

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:52.190
- Well, it actually goes back a little way

00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:54.890
when I worked at Khan Academy.

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:59.890
So I started out working on Khan Academy

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:03.830
thinking a lot about how we
get into school districts

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:07.400
around the country so I worked
as a Partnerships Manager

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.950
at Khan Academy for few years,

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:14.950
and then just after Khan Academy
acquired Duck Duck Moose,

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:20.820
which was a full profit
suite of early learning apps

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:23.260
that wanted to have even more impact

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.500
and so joined Khan Academy.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:30.200
I found the pool of
early childhood education

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:34.710
and those littlest learners so exciting

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:38.190
that I came and worked
on Khan Academy Kids.

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:42.050
And now I work on Khan Academy Kids,

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:46.840
I work on strategy and I
work on our partnerships

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:49.810
with preschools and with school districts

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:50.760
around the country.

00:02:52.990 --> 00:02:54.200
- That's great.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.800
So we often have students who are watching

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.550
and many of us are in careers that

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:03.200
maybe aren't the things
that students who are in

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.370
middle or high school think about,

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:09.380
how did you end up in
this role of partnerships

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:11.253
and linking people together?

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:16.570
- That's a good question and
I think it's something that

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:18.720
I like to talk about a little bit because

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.880
it was kind of a roundabout path

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:24.520
and it's not like when I was
in high school I thought,

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:28.040
I wanna go and work for
what I think is the best

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:31.730
ed tech company in the
world and do partnerships

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:33.503
that certainly wasn't on my radar.

00:03:35.159 --> 00:03:37.510
I grew up in Australia I
don't know if you can tell

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:38.831
from my accent.

00:03:38.831 --> 00:03:39.873
(Kristen laughs)

00:03:39.873 --> 00:03:40.706
- A little bit.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:48.230
- I had really supportive
parents who so wanted me

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:52.090
to pursue whatever I was interested in

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:54.690
and they had a really strong preference

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:58.970
for that to be medicine or the law

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:02.850
that I would maybe become
a doctor or an attorney.

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:06.060
And so I did go down that
path and became an attorney

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:10.470
in Australia and I loved
that work and at some point

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:14.130
that work brought me out to the U.S

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:16.550
and that was to study and to work

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:19.450
and so I was an international
student out here

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:22.510
doing a graduate degree and
that's when I discovered

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:26.120
Khan Academy, I thought a lot about,

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:28.660
well, what is it that I really love doing?

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:31.990
And that's connecting
people like you said,

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:33.160
it's thinking about,

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:34.890
okay, what are the big problems

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:37.810
that we should be solving and
trying to prioritize things,

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.910
because we can't quite do everything.

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:44.740
And so a job in
partnerships and in strategy

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:46.670
came to make a lot of sense,

00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:49.430
but I don't want anyone to think that

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:51.430
that was a neat path though

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:53.240
that made a lot of sense at the time.

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:55.620
There was certainly times where I thought,

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:58.680
oh gosh, I spent all this
time going to law school

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:02.104
maybe I should use that.

00:05:02.104 --> 00:05:06.270
And it's turned out that I
do, I do use my law degree

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:08.440
and I use a lot of other skills as well.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:13.440
So yeah my message would
be enjoy that journey

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:17.680
and get excited about the
fact that you might not even

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:21.760
know sitting here right now what it is

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:25.230
that you might end up really loving doing

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:26.710
in five or 10 years time,

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:29.300
which was definitely my experience.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.750
- That was totally my experience as well.

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:34.820
And I can tell a story now from where I am

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:38.690
of how I got here that sounds
like it was all a plan,

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:42.500
but it was not at any particular time,

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:44.490
there were different forks
that would have led me

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:47.590
in different directions
so I totally agree.

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:50.330
And I always like to tell
people to just be open

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:52.484
to what might come down the path

00:05:52.484 --> 00:05:55.730
as opportunities arise as well.

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:56.780
That's fascinating.

00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:58.530
I had no idea you'd been to law school

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:00.810
even though we've worked
together for a while

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:02.437
so I'm glad I asked.

00:06:02.437 --> 00:06:03.270
(Kristen laughs)

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:04.103
- Yeah.

00:06:04.103 --> 00:06:06.540
- Let's switch over to Khan Academy Kids.

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:09.510
For those who aren't familiar with it.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:10.790
Tell us a little bit about it.

00:06:10.790 --> 00:06:14.900
How is it different than
the Khan Academy main site

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:16.610
that folks go to?

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:18.040
Fill us in.

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:22.490
- Yeah, so Khan Academy Kids
is a part of Khan Academy.

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:25.220
So we all work under one umbrella

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:27.750
on the same mission of providing

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:31.070
a free world-class education
to anyone anywhere.

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:35.080
And Khan Academy Kids takes
that mission and says,

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.890
okay, in order to deliver on that

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:40.280
it's going to be really
important that kids

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:44.390
arrive at third grade able to read

00:06:44.390 --> 00:06:46.700
and able to be in the classroom

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:49.960
and feeling like they're enjoying math.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:54.150
And the way that we approach
that at Khan Academy Kids

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:58.140
is we've built a program that
covers all of those things.

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:02.030
So it's not just one subject
and it's in a mobile app,

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:04.270
which is really important
for younger learners

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:06.300
to be able to drag and drop things

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:10.730
and have something that meets their needs

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:13.060
before they can read and actually navigate

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:14.470
a desktop computer.

00:07:14.470 --> 00:07:16.460
And so I think you're
seeing some of the footage

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:19.513
of just how fun and bright and cool it is.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:22.990
But the big differences I would say

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:29.340
Khan Academy is for grades two through 12,

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:33.220
and it has math and ELA
for grades two through 12,

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:36.720
and a range of other subjects
for middle and high school,

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:41.720
Khan Academy Kids is for ages
two years to eight years.

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:44.310
So it goes up two and
through second grade,

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:46.630
getting kids ready for third grade

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:48.770
when they would move
on and use Khan Academy

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:50.500
so that's one big difference.

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:53.440
I mentioned that Khan
Academy Kids is a mobile app.

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:56.900
So the way that you
access Khan Academy Kids

00:07:56.900 --> 00:07:59.580
is through the app store that you use.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:02.420
So that could be the Apple App Store,

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:05.620
it could be Google Play,
it could even be Amazon

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:08.280
and then it would be
on your mobile device.

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:11.650
So here we can see there's
a tablet being used

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:13.190
but it could also be a mobile phone

00:08:13.190 --> 00:08:15.420
or even a Chromebook.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:20.380
Khan Academy is also available
on the App Store as an app,

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:21.980
it's a different separate app.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:24.090
So you would search for Khan Academy

00:08:24.090 --> 00:08:26.170
versus Khan Academy Kids in the App Store.

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:29.200
There are two different
apps in the App Store.

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:31.490
And Khan Academy is also
available on the web

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:35.340
so on your desktop computer,
that's one big difference.

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:38.600
I would say, though there
are more similarities

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:40.400
than there are differences.

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:44.040
The idea is to make
learning really joyful,

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:46.850
to meet learners where they're at,

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:48.700
whether they're struggling with something

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:53.520
or really accelerating and
loving a particular area

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:54.423
of their learning.

00:08:55.610 --> 00:09:00.610
And then also increasingly the
goal is to support teachers

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:02.940
and their students in classrooms

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:07.350
and both Khan Academy and Khan
Academy Kids are doing that.

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:10.670
So I think that's some
of the main similarities

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:14.883
and differences between Khan
Academy and Khan Academy Kids.

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:17.010
- I love that.

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:20.180
Yeah I usually think of it as thinking

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:22.860
we're headed towards the same goal,

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:24.830
but kids who are two
through eight years old

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:28.650
developmentally are very
different than older kids

00:09:28.650 --> 00:09:32.770
and just designing one
experience really isn't possible.

00:09:32.770 --> 00:09:36.320
And so having these two separate
experiences really gives us

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:39.460
the strength of being able
to really, as you said,

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:43.610
meet students where they are,
so love it that sounds great.

00:09:43.610 --> 00:09:46.770
So I've been poking
around in the new content

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:50.160
and I saw some new yoga videos

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:52.270
that I was really excited to see.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:55.450
There's a fun one where
they do animal poses.

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:59.770
So yoga poses that are named
after animals and all of that.

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:03.837
So with that and other
things, what have you got,

00:10:03.837 --> 00:10:06.833
what have you folks released
over the past a few months?

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:10.740
- Well, yeah, I'm glad
you noticed the yoga.

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:12.530
I'm so excited about that.

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:16.210
So Khan Academy Kids and
it's the same at Khan Academy

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:19.080
this time of year is really busy for us

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:23.440
because we are releasing
a lot of new content

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:26.370
and features in time
for the new school year,

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:29.460
so that teachers and students
can get excited about them

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:32.960
as they get learning after the summer.

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:37.350
And so we worked really hard
this past, really the past year

00:10:37.350 --> 00:10:40.370
to build a lot of new content.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:44.940
You mentioned the yoga that
was part of Khan Academy Kids

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:49.940
is really about thinking
about the whole child,

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:53.540
not just their ABCs and one, two, threes.

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:57.750
And so we've always loved
getting kids up and moving

00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:01.500
and fostering this idea that being ready

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:04.300
for kindergarten and
ready to thrive at school

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:06.470
is about more than just academics,

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:08.930
kids need to know how
to be in the classroom,

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:11.380
they need to be confident and healthy.

00:11:11.380 --> 00:11:14.830
And so we partnered with Alo Yoga

00:11:14.830 --> 00:11:18.610
and they have a part of their
program called Alo Gives.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:22.010
And Alo Gives is now fully featured

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:24.380
in the Khan Academy Kids app.

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:28.570
It's a set of videos there a few minutes,

00:11:28.570 --> 00:11:32.450
anywhere up to about five
minutes long with real people,

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:35.730
real kids, real yoga instructors
which I'm excited about.

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:38.270
- It's not Kodi Bear doing yoga.

00:11:38.270 --> 00:11:41.120
- It's not Kodi Bear doing yoga.

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:43.350
As much as we would love to see that

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:46.110
and Kodi certainly loves yoga

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:48.470
and loves to keep fit and healthy,

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:51.460
we thought our friends at Alo Gives

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:53.780
could really help show us.

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:56.891
And it's been amazing Kristen we have had

00:11:56.891 --> 00:12:01.891
lots of families sending
in the most adorable videos

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:06.430
of them all, the whole family
sometimes getting involved

00:12:06.430 --> 00:12:10.690
in doing their movement
and mindfulness each day.

00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:14.350
And for teachers, we think
this could translate well too,

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:17.330
because we're seeing lots
of teachers projecting

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:19.170
the app on their screen,

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:21.310
if they're lucky enough to
have one in their class,

00:12:21.310 --> 00:12:25.010
or if they're teaching
remotely to share their screen

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:27.760
over Zoom or whatever
platform they're using,

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:31.140
and then we can all do yoga together.

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:33.620
So it's something that
we're seeing used at home,

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:36.110
we're seeing it used a
little bit in classrooms

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:37.930
and we're just super excited about it.

00:12:37.930 --> 00:12:41.950
I know yoga is a really
important part of my life

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:45.720
and my mindfulness and so yeah,

00:12:45.720 --> 00:12:47.570
can't wait for kids to discover that.

00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:50.480
- That's fantastic.

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:54.200
So you talked about some of the new titles

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:56.090
that are available too,

00:12:56.090 --> 00:12:58.450
can you give us a little bit more detail

00:12:58.450 --> 00:13:01.150
on some of the books
that are available then?

00:13:01.150 --> 00:13:05.290
- Yeah, so big part of the latest release

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:07.850
that we're really excited
about the back to school

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:10.140
is covering second grade.

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:13.370
So we had a bunch of
kids who were just flying

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:16.440
through our app, they
were quickly running out

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:17.470
of activities.

00:13:17.470 --> 00:13:20.160
And so we couldn't keep up with them.

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:21.780
They were gonna get through

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:24.450
all of the first grade content, for sure.

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:28.170
So we have built out second grade content.

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:33.170
So we added over 200 second grade lessons.

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:37.960
We added over a 100 new animated videos

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:40.970
that are in the app and
all that animation is done

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:42.390
sort of right behind me.

00:13:42.390 --> 00:13:45.890
You can see the little
Kono where we put together

00:13:45.890 --> 00:13:47.370
the animations of our characters.

00:13:47.370 --> 00:13:51.980
So you can see Sandy the
Dingo and Peck is the bird

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:55.630
and Ollo the Elephant
and Reya the Red Panda

00:13:55.630 --> 00:13:57.310
and Kodi the Bear.

00:13:57.310 --> 00:14:00.360
Kodi narrates and takes
us through the app.

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:02.960
So added all those animations

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:05.600
that cover a range of activities.

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:09.360
We added more coloring
pages in our create section,

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:11.700
which is really, really fun.

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:13.970
We talked about the yoga that we added

00:14:13.970 --> 00:14:16.200
and we've added new books.

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:20.930
So Khan Academy Kids is a
combination of our original books

00:14:20.930 --> 00:14:23.870
that are all created here in-house

00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:26.630
and then also some partner books as well

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:28.990
and we partner with National Geographic,

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:32.020
so Young Explorer and Bellwether Media

00:14:32.020 --> 00:14:34.020
on our non-fiction books

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:36.930
and we added a ton of
new non-fiction books.

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:41.430
Some of them get really deep
in the science of things

00:14:41.430 --> 00:14:44.530
and just super interesting.

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:49.530
And so if you go into the app
and then go into the library,

00:14:50.730 --> 00:14:54.270
you will see most of the new content

00:14:54.270 --> 00:14:56.830
if you're in second grade
and you'll see these banners

00:14:56.830 --> 00:14:59.470
that say new and you'll
see the yoga videos,

00:14:59.470 --> 00:15:01.530
and you'll see the new Bellwether books,

00:15:01.530 --> 00:15:04.580
and you'll see a bunch of
new original readers as well.

00:15:04.580 --> 00:15:07.120
So we're just really excited,

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:09.520
we think we might have a
chance this year, Kristen

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:12.500
of keeping up with all those learners

00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:15.732
who are just racing through our content.

00:15:15.732 --> 00:15:17.060
(Sophie laughs)

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:19.039
- It's a good challenge to have

00:15:19.039 --> 00:15:21.697
to try and reach them
and keep up with them.

00:15:21.697 --> 00:15:25.243
That is great, excellent.

00:15:26.594 --> 00:15:29.700
So you talked about
classrooms and teachers,

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:32.360
and I know that that's been a push too.

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:35.102
What have teachers told you that they want

00:15:35.102 --> 00:15:37.893
and how have you met
some of those requests?

00:15:39.340 --> 00:15:42.440
- Yeah, well, firstly, I just got to say,

00:15:42.440 --> 00:15:44.443
and it doesn't get said enough

00:15:44.443 --> 00:15:46.590
and I think that teachers are absolutely

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:48.090
incredible and amazing.

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:51.230
We had teachers during
school closures last year

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:55.600
reaching out to us and
they were so quick to adapt

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:59.610
to online learning and they
were sharing their screen

00:15:59.610 --> 00:16:02.840
with the Khan Academy
Kids app and then we built

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:06.110
an assignment speeches
so that they could assign

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:09.930
targeted lessons for students
who were working at home

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:15.310
and then they have progress
reports where they can see

00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:17.050
what is going on.

00:16:17.050 --> 00:16:21.170
And we got a lot of
feedback when we launched

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:24.090
those features, the
assignments and the reports

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:26.520
really designed for remote
learning at the time

00:16:27.410 --> 00:16:28.770
that the teachers were enjoying it,

00:16:28.770 --> 00:16:33.300
they were loving it and
they wanted even more data

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:36.180
and they wanted even better ways

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:39.210
of assigning the right thing
to a student at the right time,

00:16:39.210 --> 00:16:41.560
which we were really happy to hear.

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:46.560
So we just launched a new
set of teacher reports

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:52.040
and so this is accessible
if you do a log into the app

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:58.060
as a teacher you'll see that
there is a assignments section

00:16:58.060 --> 00:17:01.910
and a report section and now teachers

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:04.860
can assign directly from these reports.

00:17:04.860 --> 00:17:07.040
That's one of the biggest changes we made.

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:10.000
So you can imagine if
you're a teacher and you see

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:11.630
that a student's struggling on something

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:13.090
and you want to reassign it,

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:15.540
you don't wanna go back
out into the library,

00:17:15.540 --> 00:17:19.090
find that thing and assign it
that would be really clunky.

00:17:19.090 --> 00:17:22.340
And so now you can assign
directly from this report

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:25.200
and it's really quick and easy.

00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:27.350
The other thing that
teachers were asking for was,

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:30.230
I wanna see a student's
score history on each lesson,

00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:32.550
I don't just wanna see
their latest attempt

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:35.210
or their best attempt I wanna really know

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:37.510
did they exhibit a growth mindset?

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:40.780
Did they really work
hard at mastering this?

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:44.340
How can I see the journey to
getting to that check mark,

00:17:44.340 --> 00:17:46.570
if it's a green check mark?

00:17:46.570 --> 00:17:50.690
And another big thing and
this is especially important

00:17:50.690 --> 00:17:53.600
when there has been
suspected learning loss

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:57.040
is that teachers and
parents for that matter

00:17:57.040 --> 00:18:00.850
can see how far a student has progressed

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:03.070
in a particular learning domain.

00:18:03.070 --> 00:18:04.830
So they can start to see,

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:06.990
okay, that might've been
a little bit disrupted,

00:18:06.990 --> 00:18:08.270
we spent some time out of school,

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:09.900
we spent more time outdoors,

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:11.620
we learned more things around the house

00:18:11.620 --> 00:18:15.770
all those were good things
and now it's great to have

00:18:15.770 --> 00:18:18.310
a sense of where we're at on
a particular learning domain

00:18:18.310 --> 00:18:22.810
and a learning domain might
be a component of ELA,

00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:25.350
or it might be a component of math.

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:29.350
So like counting might be
part of a learning domain

00:18:29.350 --> 00:18:32.160
and we'll get a good sense
of where a student is at.

00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:36.100
So all I can say is hats
off to our teachers,

00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:38.400
we're training them already.

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:41.830
Every year it feels like
they're even smarter

00:18:41.830 --> 00:18:45.260
about our product, Khan
Academy Kids than we are.

00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:48.810
They're teaching us a ton about
what works and what doesn't

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:50.950
when you actually take it into a classroom

00:18:50.950 --> 00:18:52.910
or virtual learning setup.

00:18:52.910 --> 00:18:56.230
And yes it's a joy.

00:18:56.230 --> 00:19:00.680
We have some Khan Academy
Kids ambassadors as well,

00:19:00.680 --> 00:19:04.860
and they are really
amazing group of teachers

00:19:04.860 --> 00:19:07.190
who are spreading the word.

00:19:07.190 --> 00:19:09.930
And to that end, if anyone listening

00:19:09.930 --> 00:19:11.450
whether you're a student or a teacher

00:19:11.450 --> 00:19:13.400
or a district administrator or a parent,

00:19:13.400 --> 00:19:18.400
or none of the above,
if you know of districts

00:19:18.820 --> 00:19:20.420
that would like to work with us,

00:19:20.420 --> 00:19:22.780
preschools, particularly
headstock preschools

00:19:22.780 --> 00:19:25.460
were so interested in reaching them.

00:19:25.460 --> 00:19:29.310
If you know teachers, if you know parents,

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:30.330
I mean, spreading the word

00:19:30.330 --> 00:19:32.460
anyone who is involved in the education

00:19:32.460 --> 00:19:34.530
of two to eight year olds should know

00:19:34.530 --> 00:19:36.373
about Khan Academy Kids, I think.

00:19:38.540 --> 00:19:39.373
- Excellent.

00:19:39.373 --> 00:19:44.220
So I know in that report
that got flashed up there

00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:47.450
on the screen for a minute to folks

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:49.610
I managed to catch that
one of the things that

00:19:49.610 --> 00:19:52.930
we talk about a lot is mastery learning.

00:19:52.930 --> 00:19:55.250
And that it's not just
about getting a score

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:56.890
on a particular assignment,

00:19:56.890 --> 00:20:00.530
but thinking about mastering a skill.

00:20:00.530 --> 00:20:03.160
And so when you're talking
about domains like counting,

00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:05.850
instead of thinking about,

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:07.310
what was my score on this assignment?

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:11.380
It's thinking about how well
do I understand counting.

00:20:11.380 --> 00:20:14.930
And it looks like your
reports are designed to help

00:20:14.930 --> 00:20:17.520
kind of teachers do both of those things,

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:19.940
understand how a student did
on a particular assignment,

00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:23.600
but also that broader
domain and understanding

00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:26.330
how they're making progress on that.

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:28.557
Is that a fair statement?

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:31.340
- Yeah that is a fair statement.

00:20:31.340 --> 00:20:35.800
And it wasn't always
that easy to aggregate up

00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:39.130
to the skill or domain
level and that was something

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:42.140
that our teachers asked for.

00:20:42.140 --> 00:20:46.920
And so that is really
part of this new release

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:49.410
that we launched just
a couple of weeks ago

00:20:49.410 --> 00:20:51.490
and that teaches us starting to use.

00:20:51.490 --> 00:20:52.780
Yeah, that's exactly right.

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:54.053
- Great, great.

00:20:55.280 --> 00:20:59.040
So you talked a little bit about last year

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:03.250
and the challenges teachers
faced and where they were.

00:21:03.250 --> 00:21:06.180
Unfortunately, it looks like
we're not out of the woods yet

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:10.390
and some of these challenges
in getting kids to school

00:21:10.390 --> 00:21:12.540
and where things are,
and I'm starting to see

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:16.540
some headlines about what
attendance is looking like

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:19.410
coming into school particularly
for young learners.

00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:21.373
What are you saying related to that?

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:27.670
- Yeah, I think we had
heard throughout the summer

00:21:27.670 --> 00:21:31.250
all about the excitement
about heading back

00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:34.860
into the classroom and we
are still really hopeful,

00:21:34.860 --> 00:21:37.200
all the amazing work that's
going on at the state

00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:40.520
and district level to make
that safe for students,

00:21:40.520 --> 00:21:43.183
I think is just incredible.

00:21:44.120 --> 00:21:49.120
There is some hesitation
when it comes to getting kids

00:21:49.570 --> 00:21:53.060
back into classrooms and we are seeing,

00:21:53.060 --> 00:21:56.290
and I think that's what you
were referencing Kristen

00:21:56.290 --> 00:22:01.290
is that the absence is really concentrated

00:22:02.030 --> 00:22:03.440
in those younger years.

00:22:03.440 --> 00:22:06.720
So I think what some of the numbers

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:09.090
coming out of places
like Stanford University

00:22:09.090 --> 00:22:11.640
in the last couple of
weeks show when it comes to

00:22:11.640 --> 00:22:16.453
enrollments in public schools is that

00:22:16.453 --> 00:22:20.880
there are lower enrollment
levels across the board,

00:22:20.880 --> 00:22:25.880
and there are even lower
enrollment levels for lower grades.

00:22:26.980 --> 00:22:31.630
And kindergarten is looking
like the hardest hit

00:22:31.630 --> 00:22:36.630
and that is really a key age
group for Khan Academy Kids.

00:22:37.340 --> 00:22:40.820
And so some of the numbers we have is that

00:22:40.820 --> 00:22:42.760
there are a million children

00:22:42.760 --> 00:22:45.810
who were expected to be enrolled

00:22:45.810 --> 00:22:50.810
who are not enrolled and not
turning up to school so far,

00:22:51.820 --> 00:22:56.560
time will tell and
close to a third of them

00:22:56.560 --> 00:22:59.530
are kindergarten students.

00:22:59.530 --> 00:23:03.600
And so I think what I can
say to folks about that

00:23:03.600 --> 00:23:08.590
is that Khan Academy Kids whether
there's learning happening

00:23:08.590 --> 00:23:12.140
at home or learning
happening in the classroom

00:23:12.140 --> 00:23:16.000
Khan Academy Kids is a
tool that can support

00:23:16.000 --> 00:23:17.890
both arrangements.

00:23:17.890 --> 00:23:21.610
So we have parents who are working

00:23:21.610 --> 00:23:26.610
on a lot of learning with
kids at home and they are able

00:23:26.760 --> 00:23:30.930
to chart the progress
of their child at home

00:23:30.930 --> 00:23:32.660
and then share it with their teacher,

00:23:32.660 --> 00:23:35.110
whether they're learning
remotely through something

00:23:35.110 --> 00:23:39.350
like Zoom, virtual school
or whether they do in fact,

00:23:39.350 --> 00:23:42.510
make it back into the classroom.

00:23:42.510 --> 00:23:47.510
And so that is one way we're
supporting parents and teachers

00:23:48.060 --> 00:23:50.550
at this time, particularly
with younger kids,

00:23:50.550 --> 00:23:53.120
particularly if they're
not ready to be back

00:23:53.120 --> 00:23:54.670
in the classroom yet.

00:23:54.670 --> 00:23:58.500
And I think we will be able
to show up on the screen here,

00:23:58.500 --> 00:24:03.500
some resources we have
here and we'll put a link

00:24:03.880 --> 00:24:06.840
in the chat and we've
got a link out there now

00:24:06.840 --> 00:24:10.720
Khan.co/KhanKids-ParentResources

00:24:12.490 --> 00:24:17.490
and this is where parents can
go to get a list of resources.

00:24:17.710 --> 00:24:22.050
And really these are around
things like structuring time.

00:24:22.050 --> 00:24:26.093
So how might a parent
plan the week or the day,

00:24:26.093 --> 00:24:30.660
there's a link there you can
see now called printables

00:24:30.660 --> 00:24:35.660
and that will link to
a bunch of activities

00:24:35.740 --> 00:24:39.050
that really go beyond
being ordinary worksheets

00:24:39.950 --> 00:24:41.330
they will link to the app.

00:24:41.330 --> 00:24:43.810
They will have activities
that are out of the app

00:24:43.810 --> 00:24:46.430
and get kids moving,
they will have cutouts,

00:24:46.430 --> 00:24:48.960
they will have craft,
they will have creativity.

00:24:48.960 --> 00:24:51.180
So you can see some of these printables

00:24:51.180 --> 00:24:53.740
are really helping parents at home

00:24:53.740 --> 00:24:58.050
because we wanna balance
that screen time on our app,

00:24:58.050 --> 00:25:02.910
learning with our characters
and working through printables.

00:25:02.910 --> 00:25:04.910
So they're just some of the ways

00:25:04.910 --> 00:25:08.350
that we're supporting
learning at home and we're-

00:25:08.350 --> 00:25:10.210
- So let me pause.

00:25:10.210 --> 00:25:13.350
Ashley Clark on YouTube hopefully
that answers your question

00:25:13.350 --> 00:25:17.170
of whether Khan Academy
Kids can be used to

00:25:17.170 --> 00:25:19.420
for parents who are
homeschooling their kids.

00:25:21.150 --> 00:25:22.620
So I didn't mean to interrupt you,

00:25:22.620 --> 00:25:24.550
but that question had just come in

00:25:24.550 --> 00:25:26.700
and thought it was right in line

00:25:26.700 --> 00:25:28.920
with what you're talking about.

00:25:28.920 --> 00:25:30.300
- Yeah, great.

00:25:30.300 --> 00:25:35.150
I think Ashley you saw that URL there

00:25:35.150 --> 00:25:37.590
reach out to us at Khan
Academy Kids Support

00:25:37.590 --> 00:25:39.990
if you have any trouble finding anything

00:25:39.990 --> 00:25:43.430
but I think the beauty of
it is it's not all in app.

00:25:43.430 --> 00:25:46.000
There's a lot going on
outside of our app as well

00:25:46.000 --> 00:25:48.160
for those little learners.

00:25:48.160 --> 00:25:51.660
And yeah, we've got a lot of parents

00:25:51.660 --> 00:25:55.380
who are relying on those
resources for a good part

00:25:55.380 --> 00:25:58.340
of their learning program
with their kids at home.

00:26:00.100 --> 00:26:01.560
- Excellent.

00:26:01.560 --> 00:26:04.370
And so let's take a look at kids

00:26:04.370 --> 00:26:07.130
who are going back into classrooms

00:26:07.130 --> 00:26:09.643
and what we can do to support them.

00:26:11.700 --> 00:26:12.533
- Yeah.

00:26:12.533 --> 00:26:14.250
Well, I think one of the big things

00:26:14.250 --> 00:26:17.310
and it sometimes feels a
little bit counterintuitive

00:26:17.310 --> 00:26:21.570
because there's a lot of stress
about learning loss going on

00:26:21.570 --> 00:26:25.420
one of the big things
that we're hearing is

00:26:25.420 --> 00:26:29.570
let's take this slow when
it comes to picking up

00:26:29.570 --> 00:26:32.410
new resources and getting
right back into learning,

00:26:32.410 --> 00:26:37.410
let's make sure kids are feeling
confident in the classroom.

00:26:37.780 --> 00:26:39.543
Everyone's been through a lot this past,

00:26:39.543 --> 00:26:41.820
more than a year now.

00:26:41.820 --> 00:26:45.730
And so we are really, really excited

00:26:45.730 --> 00:26:49.500
for kids to get back and
to meet their friends

00:26:49.500 --> 00:26:53.570
sometimes for the first time
to meet their new teacher.

00:26:53.570 --> 00:26:56.770
And then as learning begins
we're working with teachers

00:26:56.770 --> 00:27:01.350
to weave Khan Academy
Kids into the school day

00:27:01.350 --> 00:27:06.350
and into homework or work
that's done from home.

00:27:06.430 --> 00:27:10.230
And we are partnering
with school districts

00:27:10.230 --> 00:27:12.560
and we are partnering with preschools,

00:27:12.560 --> 00:27:16.020
particularly headstart
grantees across the country

00:27:16.020 --> 00:27:20.967
to support teachers and to
deliver Khan Academy Kids

00:27:21.910 --> 00:27:23.520
to as many students as possible.

00:27:23.520 --> 00:27:27.110
So if you are a school
district administrator

00:27:27.110 --> 00:27:28.620
or you know of one,

00:27:28.620 --> 00:27:33.560
you can email
KhanKidspartners@khanacademy.org,

00:27:33.560 --> 00:27:36.520
and that's where you can reach one of us

00:27:36.520 --> 00:27:40.170
who will help support
your district or preschool

00:27:40.170 --> 00:27:44.010
to get Khan Academy Kids out
there for parents and teachers

00:27:44.010 --> 00:27:46.563
and most importantly for students.

